.TH UNIMAP 1 "November 2026" "unimap 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unimap \- Unicode character map for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unimap
.RB [ \-t
.IR theme ]
.RB [ \-l ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unimap
is an interactive character map for UTF\-8 terminals.
It lists every Unicode block next to a character grid, searches characters by
name, collects characters into a text buffer and copies them to the clipboard.
.PP
Copying uses the OSC 52 terminal escape sequence and, when available,
.BR wl\-copy ,
.BR xclip ,
.B xsel
or
.BR pbcopy .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-theme " \fItheme\fR"
Start with the given color scheme. Overrides
.BR UNIMAP_THEME .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list\-themes
List the available color schemes and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.BR Tab ", " Shift\-Tab
Switch between the block list and the character grid.
.TP
.BR "Arrow keys" ", " h ", " j ", " k ", " l
Move.
.TP
.BR PgUp ", " PgDn
Move one page.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End
Start or end of the row (grid), first or last block (list).
.TP
.BR n ", " p ", " ] ", " [
Next or previous block.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " Space
Add the character to the text buffer.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete the last character from the text buffer.
.TP
.B x
Clear the text buffer.
.TP
.BR c ", " y
Copy the text buffer (or the current character if the buffer is empty) to the
clipboard.
.TP
.B g
Go to a code point (hexadecimal).
.TP
.B /
Search by character name, block name, a single character or
.BR U+XXXX .
Tab in the prompt switches between all blocks and the current block.
.TP
.BR t ", " T
Next or previous color scheme.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl\-C
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B UNIMAP_THEME
Default color scheme. Available schemes: default, dark, light,
solarized\-dark, solarized\-light, gruvbox, nord, dracula.
.SH NOTES
A UTF\-8 locale and a font containing the wanted glyphs are required.
Color schemes other than
.B default
use 24\-bit color escape sequences.
.SH AUTHOR
Kristijan Matas
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/kristijanmatas/unimap
